# Derived at publish time and uploaded as release assets — deliberately never committed.
#
# The source archive is `git archive` of the release commit and SHA256SUMS covers that archive
# plus the wheel. If either were committed, the release manifest would depend on its own digest:
# writing the file would change the tree, which would change the archive, which would change the
# sums. Keeping them derived is what makes the identity chain (build_input_commit -> released_commit
# -> wheel SHA256 -> source archive SHA256) verifiable instead of circular.
pipd-ls-sp-v0.1.0-preview.1-source.zip
SHA256SUMS
